WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.620
[intro music]

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:10.200
[crash]

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:13.220
Good morning, John it's Friday, February 2nd

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:15.935
and this is the first day that I've done a video

00:00:15.935 --> 00:00:17.351
on an even-numbered day.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.980
I also wanted to say, "Hi," to Lauren,

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:25.680
who made the first Brotherhood 2.0 reply video, on YouTube.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:27.420
Uh, well done.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.853
(beep beep) Ah! Change the battery pack?

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:31.040
That's not okay!

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:31.900
Okay!

00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:33.760
I have to do this- really quick stuff now!

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:37.020
And I wanted to say, "Hi," to all 300 of those people at the EPA Conference.

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:38.800
I'm on the way to Sarasota, Florida.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:42.200
The rest of this video will be watching what I did this morning.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:44.640
It's the opposite of the rest of my movie-magic videos.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:47.280
Where it goes...backward in time.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:50.200
You're now going forward in time at the beginning and now you're going back.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:53.460
So go back! (whispers) Go back, go back, bye.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:58.800
Some of my friends were telling me last night that my hair is sometimes a little bit messy on Brotherhood 2.0.

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:02.420
So last night...I went to bed with wet hair.

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:07.294
I haven't actually touched it yet so I wanna see what it looks like in its preserved state.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.880
Kind of a...skateboard ramp going on.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:14.140
And...like, a wave.

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:17.760
And little tufts. Tufts, like I'm a baby bird.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:21.380
I think if I touched it, it wouldn't actually even do anything.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:23.020
It's just gonna all stay there.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:28.680
Oop, okay, much worse. Much worse than it was.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:30.260
Now I look funny.

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:34.920
This is what my hair looks like now that I've touched it.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.460
I don't have time to fix it, though.

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:38.240
I'm getting ready for my next jaunt.

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:43.280
I'm in Orlando now, and I'm about to be...in...Sarasota, Florida.

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:45.440
Which is nearby Tampa, Saint Petersburg.

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:51.060
As an apology to all Orlandans who were upset by my comments that Orlando sucks-

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:52.714
actually no one seemed upset at all-

00:01:52.714 --> 00:01:56.046
I'm going to list a couple of reasons why Orlando doesn't suck.

00:01:56.046 --> 00:02:00.400
One reason is that my friend Andrew has the game Guitar Hero.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:01.701
Look how awesome I look.

00:02:01.701 --> 00:02:04.473
I'm playing David Bowie's Ziggy Stardust

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:07.720
and I am PLAYING David Bowie's Ziggy Stardust.

00:02:07.801 --> 00:02:10.061
I'm just slidin' up and down the neck.

00:02:10.061 --> 00:02:10.880
Look at me.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.254
Look at me having a good time.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:13.120
Yeah!

00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:18.500
It occurs to me that playing Guitar Hero may be another one of those things that feels cooler than it looks.

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:21.620
Another awesome thing about Orlando is Little Vietnam.

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:25.440
In Missoula, Montana, we don't really have a lot of ethnic diversity.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:29.095
And it's really nice to have a part of town, here, that's a little bit different from everywhere else.

00:02:29.820 --> 00:02:31.540
The language is a little bit different

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:33.700
and it's written on a sticky bun.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:36.600
The religious icons are a little bit different.

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:40.600
(singing) The fish are a little bit different. The smells are a little bit different.

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:44.120
The eggs are a little bit different and the lunch meat is strange!

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:47.760
(no longer singing) Generally, when I go into one of these stores, I just end up buying candy.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:50.040
And now I'm going to say my sign-off.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:51.320
I'll see you tomorrow!

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:51.880
No!

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.234
I'll see you on Monday.

